1
00:00:00,199 --> 00:00:02,369
(Penny:)If you don't stay awake,
we'll never finish.

2
00:00:02,534 --> 00:00:04,414
I'm sorry. Coffee is out of the question.

3
00:00:04,578 --> 00:00:08,458
(Sheldon:)When I moved to California, I promised my
mother that I wouldn't start doing drugs.

4
00:00:08,916 --> 00:00:10,126
(Penny:)Leonard, help.

5
00:00:10,292 --> 00:00:13,132
(Leonard:)Sheldon, we still have 380
of these things to make.

6
00:00:13,295 --> 00:00:15,885
I have faith that you will make them.
Good night.

7
00:00:16,048 --> 00:00:17,878
(Howard:)- Leonard.
- Yeah... No.

8
00:00:18,050 --> 00:00:23,890
(Leonard:)But, Sheldon, without your insight and
leadership, this enterprise will surely fail.

9
00:00:26,225 --> 00:00:28,265
(Sheldon:)You're right, of course.

10
00:00:29,103 --> 00:00:31,393
(Penny:)Here, this will help.

11
00:00:32,731 --> 00:00:34,481
(Sheldon:)Very well.

12
00:00:34,858 --> 00:00:37,238
(Sheldon:)But if this leads to opiates
or hallucinogenics...

13
00:00:37,403 --> 00:00:40,073
...you're gonna have to answer
to my mother.

14
00:00:42,199 --> 00:00:45,409
(Sheldon:)Look at Planck's constant.
People say that's arbitrary.

15
00:00:45,577 --> 00:00:48,497
That could not be less arbitrary.
If it varied even slightly...

16
00:00:48,664 --> 00:00:51,414
(Sheldon:)...life as we know it would not exist. Bam!

17
00:00:55,337 --> 00:00:59,387
(Sheldon:)Now, now, let's reconsider the entire
argument but with entropy reversed...

